            <ArticleTitle>[Embolic occlusion of the left renal artery with a non-functioning right kidney].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1003-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a 69-year-old patient with absolute arrhythmia and a rightsided non-functioning kidney embolism occurred in the left renal artery. Despite 2 1/2 days of anuria embolectomy was successful. Fastest possible restoration of renal perfusion is critical for organ preservation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
